# One image for every role in the matrix — router, peer and observer —
# because the roles differ by what they are TOLD to do, not by what they
# carry. A per-role image would let a probe fail for want of a tool and
# read as a NAT behaviour. `filter.sh` also leans on `pgrep` and `pkill`,
# which come from the base image's busybox rather than from the packages
# below; the digest pin covers them, and both call sites fail loudly if
# an applet were missing rather than reading as a class.
#
# Pinned by digest rather than by tag: this harness's whole output is a
# claim about what a NAT did, and a tag that moves under it invalidates
# the record without changing a line here. The same reason SPIKE-003 and
# SPIKE-004 phase A pin their crate versions exactly.
FROM docker.io/library/alpine@sha256:4bcff63911fcb4448bd4fdacec207030997caf25e9bea4045fa6c8c44de311d1

# nftables  — the NAT itself, and the only way to choose its mapping
#              behaviour rather than accept the kernel default.
# iproute2  — routes, and reading what address a namespace actually got.
# socat     — the probe: it exposes the observed source as
#              SOCAT_PEERADDR/SOCAT_PEERPORT, which is the measurement
#              this whole harness exists to take.
#
# PINNED BY VERSION, because the digest above does not pin these. The
# base image is fixed, but `apk add` resolves whatever the mirror serves
# at build time, and `run.sh` rebuilds every run -- so two machines, or
# one machine a month apart, could run different measurement tooling
# while every other pin in this directory held. That is the failure this
# spike's whole output is exposed to: the harness reports what a NAT did,
# and socat is what observes it.
#
# THE COST IS DELIBERATE. Alpine prunes old package versions, so when
# this release ages out the BUILD fails loudly rather than the
# measurement changing quietly. Bumping these is then a decision with a
# commit behind it, which is the same trade the dependency allow-list
# makes in CLAUDE.md §8.
RUN apk add --no-cache \
      nftables=1.1.3-r0 \
      iproute2=6.15.0-r0 \
      socat=1.8.1.3-r0
